2. In `src/interface/contentstack.ts`, add an optional `live_preview` field to `ICommonContentstackConfig` typed as `{ enable?: boolean; preview_hash?: string }` so preview context can flow through to Contentstack queries.

3. In `src/services/contentstack.ts`, add a `live_preview` block to the `Contentstack.Stack(...)` options containing `enable: true` and `preview_token: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN` — do NOT use `management_token`, and do NOT add a `host` field inside this block.

4. In `src/services/contentstack.ts`, update `setCommonConfig` (or equivalent query-config forwarding logic) to pass through the `live_preview` field from `ICommonContentstackConfig` into Contentstack query calls so preview context reaches the SDK.

5. Verify existing `Stack.setHost(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST)` logic is preserved and takes priority over `CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST` — do not modify this logic.

6. Create `test/unit/services/contentstack.test.ts` with vitest, mocking the `contentstack` module to spy on `Stack` options and `setHost` calls.

7. Add test case 1: when `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN` is set, assert Stack options include a `live_preview` block with `enable: true` and `preview_token` equal to the env value.

8. Add test case 2: when `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN` is unset, assert the `live_preview` block is absent or `preview_token` is undefined in Stack options.

9. Add test case 3: when both `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST` and `CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST` are set, assert `setHost` is called with `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST`, confirming it takes priority.

10. Run `npm test` to verify all three tests pass and no existing tests break; confirm no `host` field exists inside the `live_preview` block and `preview_token` (not `management_token`) is used.
